Ticket #4471 contains two different date bugs, not one parser bug. The export has 427 rows but
only **412 unique reports**: 15 IDs repeat because export pages overlap. Count each report ID once.

## What the reports show

Classify each report from the tenant's locale and booking form, not the intake tag. Intake guesses
from the reporter's browser; it does not identify the cause.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

### `parser` · 379 reports

The shared parser reads every date month first. Tenants in day-first locales therefore get flipped
dates. This affects all 11 tenants and arrives through app, email, and form reports.

### `hint` · 33 reports

The `booking-v3` form tells people to enter `MM/DD/YYYY`, then reads the value using the tenant's
day-first locale. Those form submissions fail differently from the shared-parser bug. The affected
tenants are Alder Physio, Copper Studio, and Pale Harbour.

<Callout kind="warn">
The desk's five one-day-move notes are all in the `parser` group. They do not make a third cause.
The intake tag also disagrees with the cause for 38 unique reports, so do not split tickets by tag.
</Callout>

## Filed tickets

- The 379 `parser` reports are recorded in [the shared-parser issue](https://github.com/ddawdaddwadawdawdawd/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1).
- The 33 `hint` reports are recorded separately in [the booking-v3 issue](https://github.com/ddawdaddwadawdawdawd/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2).

The existing incident note is at [#4471](/kb/incidents/4471). This page records the two causes
behind its merged count.

